🚩 picoCTF - Disk, disk, sleuth! II (Forensics)

📊 Challenge Information

Category: Forensics

Difficulty: Easy

Tools used: mmls, fls, icat (The Sleuth Kit)

🕵️‍♂️ Investigation Process

Method 1: The Forensic Analysis Way

Decompress the image file:

gunzip dds2-alpine.flag.img.gz


Determine the partition layout:

mmls dds2-alpine.flag.img


The Linux partition containing the filesystem starts at sector 2048.

Locate the flag file: We perform a recursive directory search (-r) on the partition:

fls -r -o 2048 dds2-alpine.flag.img


We look through the directory tree. In this challenge, the flag.txt file is tucked deeper inside the folders. Let's find its inode (e.g., 18290).

Read the flag contents:

icat -o 2048 dds2-alpine.flag.img 18290


Method 2: Command Line Shortcut

For a fast extraction, search the binary directly:

strings dds2-alpine.flag.img | grep "picoCTF"


